A1. This will take your breath away. ~ LISTERINE
A9. To spoon in a big way. ~ LADLE
A10. What clinging vines have made Harvard. ~ IVIED
A12. Encore. ~ REPEAT
A13. Covered the frame. ~ DONNED
A15. You get an awful squawk out of this kind of pipe. ~ BAG
A16. Buy-buy word. ~ AD
A17. We caught sight of this twice in Revere. ~ RE
A18. Ambition. ~ AIM
A20. No. 1 man. ~ ADAM
A22. This is always ahead of time. ~ EARLY
A26. This is delivered in a love suit by knee action. ~ PLEA
A27. What movie actresses slip on after the bath. ~ TILES
A29. S'long. ~ BYE
A30. Yummy. ~ TASTY
A31. Exclamation. ~ HO
A32. These came between Tilden and Richards in 1927. ~ NETS
A34. The Egyptians called this a lot of bull. ~ APIS
A36. This was ever thus. ~ SO
A37. How Maurice Chevalier gets gay in France. ~ GAI
A38. A heavyweight. ~ TON
A39. Dumb Dora thinks this is a member of Chic Sales' family. ~ BARGAIN
A43. The tall thing in drawers we saw standing around Macy's. ~ HIGHBOY
A48. Not the same. ~ OTHER
A49. This member is an extremist. ~ TOE
A51. Weird. ~ EERIE
A52. What the iron rule of woman is based on. ~ WHIM
A53. People willingly go here to get their hides tanned. ~ SHORE
A55. Where New Yorkers go for a cheap skate. ~ MALL
A56. A male order. ~ SON
A57. The beginning of disaster. ~ DI
A58. 490, Roman. ~ XD
A60. You'll find this in cellophane. ~ CEL
A61. Dumb Dora says what a dry girl this one turned out to be. ~ SAHARA
A64. Lit. ~ STEWED
A66. This is always on the crest of the wave. ~ LINER
A67. A mountainous maid and we don't mean Kate Smith. ~ OREAD
A68. What is the Scotchogram for "Thank you very"? ~ SANCTUARY

D1. This is considered a very doggy drink this year. ~ LAP
D2. You'll have to go to headquarters for this. ~ IDEA
D3. A little valley. ~ SLADE
D4. Tetrazzini's opening. ~ TET
D5. What a person taken for a ride in olden days did. ~ RID
D6. The way the knives are handled at the White House. ~ IVORY
D7. This will continue to be in second place in this year. ~ NINE
D8. How a poet gets even. ~ EEN
D9. This is O.K. with any lawyer. ~ LEGAL
D11. What Culbertson does when he gives himself a hand. ~ DEALS
D12. A sound investment for hard times. ~ RADIO
D14. A word that brings on fast times (plural). ~ DIETS
D15. Politicians make a cleanup in this. ~ BATH
D19. The Rochester cutup. ~ MAYO
D21. The kind of ace that is an evil to the movies. ~ MEN
D23. This got drunk at the party, looked green, and yet is supposed to make the heart grow fonder. ~ ABSINTH
D24. Crosscounty runner (abbr.). ~ RY
D25. The dressed up kid. ~ LEATHER
D26. This will make the French step. ~ PAS
D28. A big smoker held at the Algonquin club. ~ SEGAR
D30. This will help you add color to your life. ~ TINGE
D33. This sounds like Chinese to us. ~ TAI
D35. Hawaiian hash. ~ POI
D39. Fiddle sticks! ~ BOWS
D40. You'll find this sticking its head in the Aegean Sea. ~ ATHOS
D41. This is kind of nosey. ~ RHINAL
D42. Jool. ~ GEM
D44. A lowdown thing about a slip of a girl. ~ HEM
D45. Supported. ~ BRACED
D46. Cockeyed. ~ OILED
D47. This is a scream. ~ YELL
D50. Give this the double o. ~ OO
D53. This is a scream. ~ SIREN
D54. All about the big moidah! ~ EXTRA
D57. Middle name of the Gibson girl creator. ~ DANA
D59. A life member of the elks. ~ DEER
D62. Masculine pronoun. ~ HIS
D63. The highlight of olden times. ~ ARC
D64. Financial change in France. ~ SOU
D65. This will give you direction. ~ WAY


